{"result":{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["takahashi.wataru"],"name":"Takahashi, Wataru"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"2011-07-13T13:29:29Z","document_type":{"code":"a","description":"serial article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":null,"reviewer_id":null,"name":null,"sign":null},"text":"Summary: In this article, we first introduce classes of nonlinear mappings containing the class of firmly nonexpansive mappings which can be deduced from an equilibrium problem in a Hilbert space and then prove fixed point theorems and nonlinear ergodic theorems for such nonlinear mappings. Next, we define a nonlinear mapping called nonspreading which is deduced from an equilibrium problem in a Banach space and then prove fixed point theorems for such mappings in Banach spaces. In particular, we deal with the fixed point property and unbounded sets in a Banach space and solve an open problem which is connected with Ray's fixed point theorem. Furthermore, we define another nonlinear mapping called skew-nonspreading in a Banach space and then discuss duality theorems for nonlinear mappings. Using these duality theorems, we prove a fixed point theorem for skew-nonspreading mappings and obtain a necessary and sufficient condition for the existence of fixed points of skew-nonspreading mappings in a Banach space.\n\nFor the entire collection see [Zbl 1205.47003].","contribution_type":"summary"}],"id":5919703,"identifier":"1221.47097","keywords":["fixed point theorem","nonlinear ergodic theorem","equilibrium problem","nonexpansive mapping","nonspreading mapping","skew-nonspreading mapping","duality mapping"],"language":{"languages":["English"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[],"msc":[{"code":"47H09","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Contraction-type mappings, nonexpansive mappings, \\(A\\)-proper mappings, etc."},{"code":"47H10","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Fixed-point theorems"},{"code":"47H25","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Nonlinear ergodic theorems"}],"references":[],"source":{"book":[{"book_id":5834808,"isbn":[{"number":"978-4-946552-40-3","type":"hbk"}],"publisher":"Yokohama: Yokohama Publishers","year":"2010"}],"pages":"177-197","series":[],"source":"Lin, Lai Jiu (ed.) et al., Proceedings of the 9th international conference on fixed point theory and its applications (ICFPTA), Changhua, Taiwan, July 16--22, 2009. Yokohama: Yokohama Publishers (ISBN 978-4-946552-40-3/hbk). 177-197 (2010)."},"states":[["s","item with single author"],["c","is cited"]],"title":{"addition":null,"original":null,"subtitle":null,"title":"Nonlinear mappings in equilibrium problems and an open problem in fixed point theory"},"year":"2010","zbmath_url":"https://zbmath.org/5919703"},"status":{"execution":"successful request","execution_bool":true,"internal_code":"ok","last_id":null,"nr_total_results":1,"nr_request_results":1,"query_execution_time_in_seconds":0.09096312522888184,"status_code":200,"time_stamp":"2026-05-12T11:40:03Z"}}